Consider the set of functions \emph{H} : \emph{X →Y} for sets \emph{X}
and \emph{Y}, denoted by \emph{HX,Y}. Consider a weight assignment
\emph{D} on \emph{HX,Y}. Let \emph{W ⊆X}. We define the marginal weight
