\begin{quote}
the state of \emph{A} before the \emph{i}th query, and
\end{quote}

\emph{HUi−}1\emph{H...U}1\emph{HU}0\emph{\textbar x⟩}

\begin{quote}
the state after the \emph{i}th query. The final state of the algorithm
is
\end{quote}

\emph{UqH...U}1\emph{HU}0\emph{\textbar x⟩}

\begin{quote}
We say that a quantum algorithm is efficient if \emph{q} is a
polynomial, and all the \emph{Ui} are composed of
\end{quote}

a polynomial number of universal basis gates (the Hadamard, CNOT, and
